{
  "case_id": "2017-17-530",
  "document_hash": "5bc751829d164033b2750ffaf4d70747a7e1ca1c65ab537d020e8c44313412af",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-530",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "5bc751829d164033b2750ffaf4d70747a7e1ca1c65ab537d020e8c44313412af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bc751829d16-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:05 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Wisconsin Central (Petitioners)",
      "case_id": "2017-17-530",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "5bc751829d164033b2750ffaf4d70747a7e1ca1c65ab537d020e8c44313412af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bc751829d16-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We believe it is not for a simple reason. Stock is not money. The plain meaning of \"money\" is a generally accepted medium of exchange. And stock is not that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-17-530",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "5bc751829d164033b2750ffaf4d70747a7e1ca1c65ab537d020e8c44313412af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bc751829d16-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How about -- how about a check?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Wisconsin Central (Petitioners)",
      "case_id": "2017-17-530",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "5bc751829d164033b2750ffaf4d70747a7e1ca1c65ab537d020e8c44313412af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bc751829d16-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There was a report cited in our papers in the National Industrial Conference that talked about how, going back to the 19th century, many railroads offered stock purchase plans to their employees. So it certainly was a well-recognized form of remuneration back when the statute was enacted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-17-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bc751829d164033b2750ffaf4d70747a7e1ca1c65ab537d020e8c44313412af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bc751829d16-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: I guess I'm still waiting for a difference that would -- would -\u00ad would match why Congress would make this different treatment of stock options."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dupree",
      "case_id": "2017-17-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bc751829d164033b2750ffaf4d70747a7e1ca1c65ab537d020e8c44313412af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bc751829d16-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DUPREE: Well, I -- I think the different treatment of stock options traces back to the original decision that Congress made and that it has maintained now in the statutory text for 70-plus years, the distinction between a broad wage-based tax system in FICA that encompasses pretty much everything the employee gets and the far narrower tax base that the railroad system utilizes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bc751829d164033b2750ffaf4d70747a7e1ca1c65ab537d020e8c44313412af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bc751829d16-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It has much higher tax rates. I mean, the railroad combined tax rate is north of 30 percent, whereas FICA is about 14 percent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bc751829d164033b2750ffaf4d70747a7e1ca1c65ab537d020e8c44313412af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bc751829d16-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I thought -- I thought that the railroad pension system in the 1930s was at risk. That was one of the reasons why this scheme was developed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-17-530",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "5bc751829d164033b2750ffaf4d70747a7e1ca1c65ab537d020e8c44313412af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bc751829d16-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Is a third -- a third possibility that the employee waits until after he or she retires and doesn't receive the big salary and then exercises the option?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dupree",
      "case_id": "2017-17-530",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "5bc751829d164033b2750ffaf4d70747a7e1ca1c65ab537d020e8c44313412af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bc751829d16-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DUPREE: Thank you. Just a few points. The first is this Court obviously needs to construe this tax provision in the context of the code as a whole. We identify numerous provisions in the code, both as it existed during the Great Depression but also as it exists today, that makes clear that when Congress uses the word \"money\" in a tax statute, it does not mean stock."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-530",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "5bc751829d164033b2750ffaf4d70747a7e1ca1c65ab537d020e8c44313412af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bc751829d16-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF THOMAS H. DUPREE, JR. ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONERS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-530",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "5bc751829d164033b2750ffaf4d70747a7e1ca1c65ab537d020e8c44313412af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bc751829d16-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: How many of those other code provisions use the words \"money remuneration\" as opposed to just \"money\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2017-17-530",
